1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,680
From this tower you see two roads that cross.

2
00:00:03,630 --> 00:00:12,393
One car travels east at ninety kilometers per hour, and another travels south at sixty, and both are heading toward the intersection.

3
00:00:12,393 --> 00:00:16,223
Play the time or move the slider to watch them advance.

4
00:00:16,223 --> 00:00:22,872
The distances from each car to the intersection decrease, and that is why their derivatives are negative.

5
00:00:22,872 --> 00:00:30,226
The graph shows the distance between the two cars, and the slope of its tangent is the rate at which they approach each other.

6
00:00:30,226 --> 00:00:39,148
With Go to the instant you place yourself at the moment when the first car is two hundred meters from the intersection and the second is one hundred and fifty.

7
00:00:39,148 --> 00:00:43,005
Then turn on Reveal answer to check your calculation.

